{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/349188-shamanism-the-lunar-style-of-sorcery","id":349188,"title":"Shamanism - the Lunar style of sorcery?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-24T12:04:48-08:00","id":349188,"title":"Shamanism - the Lunar style of sorcery?","content":"<a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalted_3E:_What_We_Know#Sorcery_.2F_Necromancy_.2F_Thaumaturgy\" target=\"_blank\">http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/m...2F_Thaumaturgy</a><br /> <br /> I'm going back through the first Lunar manual; it spent its storytelling chapter on &quot;barbarians&quot;, so the lexicon and chapter explain the terms of &quot;shaman&quot;, &quot;chiminage&quot;, &quot;taboo&quot; and &quot;god&quot;. Basically, a shaman is a client who provides worship or performs work (&quot;chiminage&quot;) for a supernatural figure in exchange for knowledge, protection or blessings. Worship often takes the form of prohibited behaviors (&quot;taboo&quot;).<br /> <br /> The Shaping Actions required to gather power for necromancy-style spells likely involves blood-sacrifice; necessarily, this makes playing a necromancer extremely different from playing a vanilla sorceror even if they're using the same spells.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Lunars or anyone who pursues shamanism-style sorcery can gather power through performing worship or acts of service for spirits appropriate to the kind of spell one wishes to cast?<br /> <br /> Perhaps this might have a benefit in allowing a shaman to set up multiple spells ahead of time, as &quot;favors&quot; already &quot;owed&quot; to him by various &quot;gods&quot; which he can cash in whenever this or that spell becomes suitable to his situation?<br /> <br /> Maybe there might be taboos which prohibit certain actions that would void the &quot;favor&quot; and erase the power gathered for the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-24-2014, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T12:14:49-08:00","id":349211,"title":"","content":"I suspect one of the sorcery initiations available to mortals will work like this and Sidereals might be able to do something similar, but worshiping gods isn't something I see Lunars doing. <br /> <br /> For Lunar sorcery, I suspect casting spells at night, animal sacrifices, the consumption of alcohol and narcotics and exposure to extreme weather would be more appropriate shape sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T12:27:42-08:00","id":349218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/349188-shamanism-the-lunar-style-of-sorcery?p=349211#post349211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect one of the sorcery initiations available to mortals will work like this and Sidereals might be able to do something similar, but worshiping gods isn't something I see Lunars doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trading favors for Gifts is something the Garou did. Lunars have Charms instead of Gifts, but power for spellcasting is an acceptable form of payment.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't have to the Lunar's worship, necessarily. The Lunar might simply get a tribe of mortals to do the worshiping for him, acting as their intermediary between men and gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T13:08:01-08:00","id":349234,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind a style or initiation of Sorcery in which your shaping actions rely on various more direct forms of invocation. I would be a bit unsure of this being a default form for Lunars, and wouldn't entirely think much of it being called shamanism. I'm not sure I even care much for riding too heavily on distinguishing terms for different kinds of spiritual figure, but if it's needed I say keep it simple; shamans are people who use ecstatic methods for altered state of consciousness to approach the occult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T17:28:38-08:00","id":349406,"title":"","content":"I'd rather go with Isator's suggestion about altered states of consciousness than invoking Gods.<br /> The reason for this, is that in Exalted, you talk to Gods all the time anyway. So a Shaman is going to be someone with Eyes of the Cat. It'd seem weird to be chatting to Gods and asking them for favours all the time, as my own No Moon Mongol-esque Shaman often does, and then cast a spell and pray for favours in an entirely different way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T17:59:06-08:00","id":349430,"title":"","content":"I may have mis-emphasized things, because people seem hung up on &quot;Lunar begs god for spell&quot; instead of &quot;hey Bob, I need a spell; you have an errand that needs doing around here? Let's make a deal.&quot;<br /> <br /> More like a bargain between equals, because the Lunar is a demigod hero, not a mortal worshiper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T22:15:40-08:00","id":349567,"title":"","content":"My issue with this is that it becomes vey much a relationship to be managed, whereas channeling rituals as I understand them are very much of the 'action in, motes out' variety. You might gather ambient Essence, or perform blood sacrifices, or channel energy from an object but they're what we would have thought of as Simple actions, things you do n9w for immediate result ... even if you might have to stack a few ti charge your spell up.<br /> <br /> The 'remember when I tended your shrine last week' model lacks this immediacy and introduces a whole bunch of complications. Does it allow shamans to bank a large amount of power from months of shrine-tending? If you really need to cast a spell now can you go into shrine-tending debt? What if either side reneges? Can they even? Does providing this pover effect the God, negatively or otherwise? <br /> <br /> I've played a lot of spirit-speakers and priests and I tend to think that the relationship between spirits and mortals is rich and dynamic and best played out over the long term in reference to the specific purview and powers of the Gods in question. This is especially true when thauturmagy and the Occult ability are used well (which, certainly, isn't always the case).<br /> <br /> I don't think the relationship is particularly helped by adding 'generic battery for spells' to the boons Gods can provide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T22:30:17-08:00","id":349576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/349188-shamanism-the-lunar-style-of-sorcery?p=349567#post349567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue with this is that it becomes vey much a relationship to be managed, whereas channeling rituals as I understand them are very much of the 'action in, motes out' variety. You might gather ambient Essence, or perform blood sacrifices, or channel energy from an object but they're what we would have thought of as Simple actions, things you do n9w for immediate result ... even if you might have to stack a few ti charge your spell up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two of the five &quot;initiation paths&quot; in the corebook involve having a bargain or relationship with a supernatural being. 3E Sorcery handles that stuff with no problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T22:33:44-08:00","id":349577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/349188-shamanism-the-lunar-style-of-sorcery?p=349576#post349576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two of the five &amp;quot;initiation paths&amp;quot; in the corebook involve having a bargain or relationship with a supernatural being. 3E Sorcery handles that stuff with no problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! So much for me then ... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T22:49:58-08:00","id":349581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/349188-shamanism-the-lunar-style-of-sorcery?p=349576#post349576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two of the five &quot;initiation paths&quot; in the corebook involve having a bargain or relationship with a supernatural being. 3E Sorcery handles that stuff with no problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Three, isn't it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually I guess one of them is kind of up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T22:51:15-08:00","id":349597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/349188-shamanism-the-lunar-style-of-sorcery?p=349576#post349576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two of the five &quot;initiation paths&quot; in the corebook involve having a bargain or relationship with a supernatural being. 3E Sorcery handles that stuff with no problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought there were six initiations... Or did you leave out the one where you can do it because you're a Solar?<br /> Do these Initiation paths have any influence on the way Sorcery works, or is it just flavor-text?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T22:53:11-08:00","id":349599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/349188-shamanism-the-lunar-style-of-sorcery?p=349597#post349597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there were six initiations... Or did you leave out the one where you can do it because you're a Solar?<br /> Do these Initiation paths have any influence on the way Sorcery works, or is it just flavor-text?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have influence, yes, but they're also very obviously examples that can be reassembled into new shapes if you don't like 'em as written. The corebook is not like &quot;IF YOU ARE A SORCERER YOU MUST FIT ONE OF THESE FIVE ARCHETYPES.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T22:57:20-08:00","id":349604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/349188-shamanism-the-lunar-style-of-sorcery?p=349597#post349597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there were six initiations... Or did you leave out the one where you can do it because you're a Solar?</div> </div> </div> </div>John wanted to save one of them for later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do these Initiation paths have any influence on the way Sorcery works, or is it just flavor-text? </div> </div> </div>Your &quot;path&quot; will give you ways of gathering Essence to shape spells other than the default options. If you want to go beyond just that, there are options your &quot;path&quot; lets you pursue. Definitely not just flavor text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T22:58:39-08:00","id":349605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/349188-shamanism-the-lunar-style-of-sorcery?p=349604#post349604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">John wanted to save one of them for later.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's not like the book is in danger of running under wordcount. (Yeesh!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T23:18:03-08:00","id":349618,"title":"","content":"How many words devoted to sorcery?<br /> <br /> It's okay to ballpark this figure, I'm just curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T23:33:04-08:00","id":349639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/349188-shamanism-the-lunar-style-of-sorcery?p=349618#post349618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many words devoted to sorcery?<br /> <br /> It's okay to ballpark this figure, I'm just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>About 20k words in the latest version of the draft I have, but it's possible that stuff has been cut/Lea's editing has